WQ-02: give check-valve pipes volume and reactions in water quality

initsegs() creates the initial volume segment only for links of type
PIPE, and reactpipes() skips every link that is not of type PIPE. A
pipe with a check valve has type CVPIPE (0), so it gets no segment and
no reactions: water crosses it instantly and unchanged. Test for
Type <= PIPE, as setreactflag() and the rest of the code base do for
"any pipe".

Apply from the root of an EPANET checkout at 83e25bb:
    git apply WQ-02_fix.patch

diff --git a/src/qualreact.c b/src/qualreact.c
index 7ce6234..29dbff8 100644
--- a/src/qualreact.c
+++ b/src/qualreact.c
@@ -134,7 +134,7 @@ void reactpipes(Project *pr, long dt)
     for (k = 1; k <= net->Nlinks; k++)
     {
         // Skip non-pipe links (pumps & valves)
-        if (net->Link[k].Type != PIPE) continue;
+        if (net->Link[k].Type > PIPE) continue;
         rsum = 0.0;
         vsum = 0.0;
 
diff --git a/src/qualroute.c b/src/qualroute.c
index 2309ba8..2eed339 100644
--- a/src/qualroute.c
+++ b/src/qualroute.c
@@ -583,7 +583,7 @@ void initsegs(Project *pr)
     {
         qual->FirstSeg[k] = NULL;
         qual->LastSeg[k] = NULL;
-        if (net->Link[k].Type == PIPE)
+        if (net->Link[k].Type <= PIPE)
         {
             v = LINKVOL(k);
             j = net->Link[k].N2;
